## Task 2

My evaluation will ask whether the interactive calendar helps people compare parking availability faster and more accurately than the static clocks. My hypothesis is that the ability to select dates will help reduce completion time and increase accuracy. Each participant will use both versions and answer two questions for each. 

**Set A:**
1. At the gym, which date had the larger increase in percentage available from its first to last recorded visit: October 7 or October 9? 
**Correct Answer:** October 7.

2. At school, which date had the larger decrease in availability between 09:00 and 16:00: October 22 or October 23?? 
**Correct Answer:** October 22.


**Set B:**
1. At the gym, which date had the larger increase in percentage available from its first to last recorded visit: October 12 or October 14? 
**Correct Answer:** October 14.

2. At school, which date had the larger decrease in availability between 09:00 and 16:00: October 26 or October 27?
**Correct Answer:** October 26.


These questions require comparing changes across two dates. This allows me to see if the calendar speeds up finding different dates and observations.

Five participants will start with the static view and five will start with the interactive view. P01–P03 will use static with Set A, then interactive with Set B. P04–P05 will use static with Set B, then interactive with Set A. P06–P07 will use interactive with Set A, then static with Set B. P08–P10 will use interactive with Set B, then static with Set A. This is so the participants don't memorize their answers from the previous set. Everyone will receive the same explanations and instructions. Participants will select one of the dates as their final answer. Participants will be timed and the timer stops when they record their final answer. Correct answers receive 1 point. Incorrect answers receive 0. I will record anonymous IDs, question variants, answers, accuracy, completion times, and observations. This will be a remote study. Particpants will submit CSV and feedback on google form after completion.
